---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Krize Kster" description="I'm Krishna Soni, founder and CEO of Kri Zek, working out of Jaipur.">
  <head slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Krishna Soni",
      "alternateName": ["Krize Kster", "Krizekster"],
      "jobTitle": "Founder & CEO",
      "worksFor": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Kri Zek"
      },
      "sameAs": [
        "https://www.linkedin.com/in/krizekster/",
        "https://www.linkedin.com/company/kri-zek",
        "https://www.krizek.tech/",
        "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=tech.krizek.alteredbrilliance",
        "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/kri-zek-llc",
        "https://happenstance.ai/u/krizekster",
        "https://www.instagram.com/krizekster/",
        "https://www.instagram.com/krizek.tech/",
        "https://www.instagram.com/krizekindia/",
        "https://github.com/krizekster",
        "https://dev.to/krizekster",
        "https://thepowerofgaming.hashnode.dev"
      ]
    })} />
  </head>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About / 01</p>
    <h1 data-parallax="0.04">Building with intention at the edge of play and cognition.</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>I'm <strong>Krishna Soni</strong>, founder and CEO of <strong>Kri Zek</strong>, working out of Jaipur.</p>
      <p>I spent four years as a game developer before starting the company, and the whole time I kept running into the same thing: games are the most sophisticated behavioral instruments ever built, and nobody treats them that way. Every decision inside a game is a projection of the mind making it. How you allocate scarce resources. How fast you abandon a failing strategy. How long it takes you to recover after a loss. Conventional cognitive testing measures none of this well, because the moment someone knows they are being tested, the behavior stops being real.</p>
      <p>So I wrote the book, published the research, and built the algorithm.</p>
      <p>Kri Zek runs across two entities, <strong>KRI ZEK LLC</strong> in Delaware and <strong>Krizek India Private Limited</strong> in Jaipur, and the work splits three ways: <em>Altered Brilliance</em> as the product, <em>tGiX™</em> as the measurement layer underneath it, and <em>Codename TGX-1</em> as the model being trained on what that layer collects.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-line bg-[#e4e9df]">
    <div class="section-wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.75fr_1.25fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The path so far</p>
        <h2 data-parallax="0.03" class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5.2rem)] font-extrabold leading-[.84] tracking-[-.09em]">A practice, not a finish line.</h2>
      </div>
      <Timeline />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Working principles</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.03" class="section-heading mt-3">Good work has a point of view.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <Card title="Useful over noisy" tag="01 / Principle" subtitle="Product thinking" accent="green">
        <p>Technology earns its place when it removes friction and makes the next decision easier. The best solutions tend to be clear before they are clever.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Systems are human" tag="02 / Principle" subtitle="Engineering" accent="blue">
        <p>Behind every architecture is a person trying to do meaningful work. Reliability, clarity, and empathy belong together.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Curiosity compounds" tag="03 / Principle" subtitle="Craft" accent="steel">
        <p>Writing, games, watches, and software all reward close attention. The most interesting ideas often live at the edges between disciplines.</p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
